{
 "type": "FeatureCollection",
 "name": "swiss_foehn_flow_lines_topo",
 "description": "Foehn flow lines digitised from a schematic map image (south foehn = red arrows, north foehn = blue arrows; lines run from tail to arrow tip). Georeferenced by matching the map's rivers, lakes and national border to swisstopo swissTLMRegio 2026 (2nd-order polynomial, residual ~400 m = 1 map pixel), then each line snapped to the valley floors / saddles of the Copernicus GLO-30 DEM within 2.5 km of its drawn position, centred on flat valley floors and lakes. 'from_near'/'to_near' are the nearest towns, for orientation only. Afterwards some lines were edited by hand in QGIS (2026-11-20).",
